# SGLang GPU

When the user asks to deploy, install, or serve a model with **SGLang** on a **GPU server** (including a blank or unconfigured host), follow skill `sglang-gpu`. Read its `SKILL.md` and run it. Do not invent a parallel Docker or CUDA install.

vLLM is `vllm-gpu`. Local Ollama / Qdrant compose is `llm-infra`. If skill `sglang-gpu` is not installed, say so.
